* MathFn3 component reference -- the "## Example" netlist verbatim.
* No title line -- see doc-verify/const/example.cir's own comment for why.
*
* SEL is if: in1 = 1 > 0.5 selects the "then" branch, so SEL = THEN = 10. L is limit: it
* clamps in1 = 5 to the span of in2/in3 = [0, 2], so L = 2. See
* test_mathfn.py::test_example_fn3_if_select_and_limit_clamp.
CND kind=const value=1
THEN kind=const value=10
ELSE kind=const value=20
SEL kind=if in1=CND in2=THEN in3=ELSE
V kind=const value=5
LO kind=const value=0
HI kind=const value=2
L kind=limit in1=V in2=LO in3=HI
